      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain the difference between high glycemic index and low glycemic index foods? specifically why it matters for insulin.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Glycemic index (GI) foods, like those with a high GI, are rapidly digested, causing a quick spike in blood sugar. This sudden surge forces your pancreas to release a large amount of insulin to manage the sugar. Conversely, low GI foods release glucose slowly, leading to a more gradual rise in blood sugar and a steadier insulin response. This difference is crucial because constant, high insulin spikes can be problematic for long-term health, especially for those managing blood sugar.",
