    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so if i'm trying to keep my levels stable, should i be looking for foods with a lower index? can you give me some examples of high and low GI foods so i know what to look for at the grocery store?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, absolutely, focusing on lower GI foods is generally the best strategy for keeping your blood sugar levels stable. Think of it like a slow, steady stream versus a sudden flood of energy. For high GI foods, you'll find things like white bread, sugary cereals, and white rice. In contrast, low GI options include whole grains like oats and barley, most vegetables, and legumes such as lentils and beans.",
      "source": "target",
