    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. one more thing, how do things like fruit fit into this? i know they have sugar but i hear they're healthy. is there a way to eat them without causing a massive spike?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Fruit is a tricky one, as it contains natural sugars, but it's not all bad, especially when you consider the fiber! The fiber in fruit acts like a buffer, slowing down the rate at which that sugar enters your bloodstream. To minimize a spike, it's best to eat whole fruit rather than drinking fruit juice, which is pure, fast-acting sugar. Furthermore, pairing fruit with a source of healthy fat or protein, like nuts or yogurt, can further slow down digestion.",
      "source": "target",
